      "title": "Handling Unresponsive Services and Duplicate Tickets",
      "content_summary": "Guidelines for triaging unresponsive services and closing duplicate tickets when insufficient information is available.",
      "content_body": "When a service is unresponsive or exhibits intermittent failure, first verify if the ticket is a duplicate of an existing issue. If it is, close the duplicate ticket immediately. If no duplicate exists and there is insufficient information to determine the root cause, request specific details such as timestamps, affected URLs, and browser versions. If the user's issue is due to operator error or unsupported configuration, provide customer education resources. Escalate to engineering only if the issue persists and cannot be resolved with configuration changes."
